cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite the article below (the preferred
  citation). You may additionally cite the software itself.
title: SeqVerify
abstract: >-
  SeqVerify is a Python-based command line tool for analysis of whole genome 
  sequencing data for gene-editing verification. It performs insertion site 
  detection, copy number variation (CNV) analysis through CNVPytor, bacterial 
  contamination detection through KRAKEN2 and BRACKEN, and variant calling and 
  filtering aided by SnpEff and SnpSift.
type: software
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
repository-code: "https://github.com/mpiersonsmela/SeqVerify"
url: "https://github.com/mpiersonsmela/SeqVerify"
